# --- uniXNU device adaptation: the video console must find our GOP framebuffer ---------------
# sheng's DarwinBoot equivalent passes the framebuffer base with the low-bit "physical" marker
# XNU expects; ours hands over a clean physical address (0xE3940000), so initialize_screen()
# treats it as a virtual address and never maps it. Without these two the kernel reaches
# vcattach(), decides there is no video, switches to a serial console this board does not have,
# and every kprintf is dropped. Taken verbatim from the iOS 17 line
# (UniXNU-uke/patches/xnu/zzzzz-video-console-physical-fb.patch and zzzzzz-video-console-text.patch).
uke-video-console-physical-fb.patch
uke-video-console-text.patch

